WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.580
"When you're setting up a campaign with manual keyword targeting, the match type determines

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:12.041
how closely the keywords you bid on match the shopping queries customers are using.

00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:12.360
Because

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.480
broad match gives you the highest traffic exposure of any of the match types, it's

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.380
best for driving awareness or to learn which terms customers use, helping you refine campaigns

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:21.970
later on.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.100
Let's take the example of a set of blue cotton sheets that you're advertising

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.148
and you've included blue cotton sheets in your keywords.

00:00:29.148 --> 00:00:31.180
This one keyword is a combination

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.775
of three terms – blue, cotton and sheets.

00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:36.740
If you're using the broad match type, your

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.800
ad may display when customers browse using all three of those terms in any order, plus

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.486
close variations like plurals.

00:00:43.486 --> 00:00:47.700
If customers use other terms along with these anywhere in

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.180
their queries, your ad may also appear.
 (

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.000
upbeat music)
